>Am I right in thinking that NetHack does not have such a function?

Yes.

>I'm
>not going to suggest one gets implemented (that would have been done
>ages ago if the DevTeam felt it was desirable, I'm sure), but I would
>like to know just how I am supposed to figure out monsters stats and
>properties in NetHack without reading spoilers or diving into the
>source.

There are three items - two magical, one not - that permit one to
observe certain attributes of a monster to which they are applied.  The
non-magical one always appears in the starting inventory of a certain
character class. Of the magical ones, one is an artifact weapon and the
other is a wand.

Beyond that, all you can do is observe which attacks perform the best
against which opponents.
